#[$in title:["Generics"]]
#[$in description:["Declaration-site generics, type application and local inference in Moth."]]
#[$in head:[language_theme_head]]

#[navbar]
#[sidebar]
init_docs_sidebar()!
#[section, $md:
    # Generics

    Generics let one declaration describe a family of concrete structs, choices
    or functions. Moth specialises each use statically and doesn't expose erased
    generic values at runtime.

Ordinary type inference uses immediate arguments and receiving types. A
bounded numeric-origin exception can carry an existing numeric value through
a generic signature to later exact uses in the same body. It never searches
callee bodies or the whole program.
]

